---
/**
 * The AEP archive (HAUSSMANN P3.5 O1; ADR-055 §7, ratified 2026-08-20).
 *
 * Tables-first, per the anatomy shared by all four process-primary exemplars in the reference
 * corpus (PEPs, TC39, EIPs, W3C Process) — the table IS the page, not a summary above prose.
 *
 * EVERY COUNT ON THIS PAGE IS DERIVED FROM THE COLLECTION (campaign convention 1 / WebForge
 * KW-14). Nothing here is typed. That is not decoration: ADR-055 §8's honest-youth posture is
 * only credible if the occupancy figures cannot be flattered, and a typed count is exactly the
 * defect this campaign exists to end.
 */
import DocumentationLayout from '../../../layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/sections/Callout.astro';
import { getSortedProposals, STATE_MACHINE, statusCounts } from '../../../utils/proposals';
import { buildCollectionPageJsonLD } from '../../../utils/seo';

const proposals = await getSortedProposals();
const counts = statusCounts(proposals);
const total = proposals.length;

// The lowest unassigned number — derived, so the sentence about occupancy cannot drift.
const nextNumber = total === 0 ? 1 : Math.max(...proposals.map((p) => p.data.number)) + 1;

const jsonLD = buildCollectionPageJsonLD({
  title: 'aDNA Enhancement Proposals',
  description: 'The numbered public record of proposed changes to the aDNA standard.',
  url: Astro.url.href,
});
---

<DocumentationLayout
  title="Proposals"
  description="The numbered public record of proposed changes to the aDNA standard — including the ones that were turned down."
  jsonLD={jsonLD}
>
  <p>
    Changes to the aDNA standard are proposed as numbered <strong>aDNA Enhancement Proposals</strong>.
    The process is described by <a href="/community/proposals/aep-1/">AEP-1</a>, which is itself a
    proposal, filed through the process it describes.
  </p>

  <p>
    Numbers are permanent. A proposal that is rejected or withdrawn keeps its number and stays on this
    page, so what the project turned down is as readable as what it adopted.
  </p>

  <h2 id="archive">The archive</h2>

  {total === 0 ? (
    <p>No proposals have been filed yet.</p>
  ) : (
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="aep-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">All aDNA Enhancement Proposals, by number</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">#</th>
            <th scope="col">Title</th>
            <th scope="col">Status</th>
            <th scope="col">Author</th>
            <th scope="col">Sponsor</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {proposals.map((p) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="aep-num">
                <a href={`/community/proposals/aep-${p.data.number}/`}>AEP-{p.data.number}</a>
              </td>
              <td>
                <a href={`/community/proposals/aep-${p.data.number}/`}>{p.data.proposal_title}</a>
              </td>
              <td>
                <span class={`aep-status aep-status-${p.data.status}`}>{p.data.status}</span>
              </td>
              <td>{p.data.authors.join(', ')}</td>
              <td>{p.data.sponsor ?? <span class="aep-none">none</span>}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  )}

  <h2 id="states">The states</h2>
  <p>
    Every proposal is in exactly one of eight states. Occupancy below is counted from the archive above,
    not asserted — which is why most rows read zero.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="aep-table">
      <caption class="sr-only">The eight proposal states, their meanings, and how many proposals are in each</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">State</th>
          <th scope="col">Meaning</th>
          <th scope="col">Terminal</th>
          <th scope="col">Currently</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {STATE_MACHINE.map((s) => (
          <tr>
            <td><span class={`aep-status aep-status-${s.id}`}>{s.id}</span></td>
            <td>{s.meaning}</td>
            <td>{s.terminal ? 'yes' : 'no'}</td>
            <td class="aep-count">{counts[s.id]}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    A terminal state is terminal for that number. A revived idea returns as a new proposal that names the
    one it descends from; the old number keeps its old outcome.
  </p>

  <h2 id="file">How to file one</h2>
  <p>
    Open a change proposal on the
    <a href="https://github.com/aDNA-Network/aDNA/issues/new?template=change_proposal.md" rel="noopener">aDNA repository</a>.
    If the change is <em>normative</em> — if it alters what the standard requires of a conforming vault —
    it becomes an AEP and is numbered here. If it does not, it stays an ordinary issue or pull request,
    which is faster for everyone.
  </p>
  {/* The two links below MUST point at the image repo, not the dev vault: gate-14's C-1 rule
      forbids proof-links to aDNA-Network/aDNA.aDNA, and it is right — the image is the install
      target and the door the site advertises. Both files are added to the image repo in the same
      increment (ADR-055 ⊳ D-J / R-122); if that push does not land, these links come out before
      deploy rather than shipping dead. */}
  <p>
    Agents may author proposals, and every proposal discloses whether one did. Only a human can ratify:
    no proposal reaches <code>accepted</code> without a named person and a date. The
    <a href="https://github.com/aDNA-Network/aDNA/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md" rel="noopener">contribution guide</a>
    covers the non-normative routes, and participation is governed by the
    <a href="https://github.com/aDNA-Network/aDNA/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md" rel="noopener">code of conduct</a>.
  </p>

  <Callout variant="info" title="The state of this process">
    <p>
      The process began on 20 August 2026. There {total === 1 ? 'is' : 'are'} <strong>{total}</strong>
      {total === 1 ? ' proposal' : ' proposals'} on record and the next number to be assigned is
      <strong>AEP-{nextNumber}</strong>. There is no published median review time here because none has
      been measured yet; when there is enough history to compute one, it will appear.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</DocumentationLayout>

<style>
  /* Tokens only — AA in both themes, no hardcoded colour (gate-25 token discipline). */
  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .aep-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .aep-table th,
  .aep-table td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .aep-table thead th {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .aep-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .aep-count {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-align: right;
  }

  .aep-none {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Status is carried by the WORD, not by colour — the colour is a second channel only
     (gate-18 categorical-colour discipline: never colour-alone). */
  .aep-status {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    padding: 0.1em 0.5em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .aep-status-final,
  .aep-status-accepted {
    border-color: var(--color-primary);
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .aep-status-rejected,
  .aep-status-withdrawn {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
